# Make (or repair) the one test login an agent can use to actually open a screen.
#
# WHY A WORKFLOW AND NOT A LOCAL SCRIPT. Creating a login needs the Supabase
# management token, and no developer machine here holds one — GitHub does, as the
# repo secret SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN, which is how deploy-backend.yml ships the
# backend. So this is the only place the privileged half can run. The unprivileged
# half — signing in as the account afterwards — needs nothing but the password,
# which is why the password is chosen OUTSIDE this workflow and handed to it.
#
# HOW THE PASSWORD GETS HERE, AND HOW A LOCAL AGENT KNOWS IT. The value is not
# generated in CI, deliberately: anything invented inside a run can only leave it
# through a log or an artifact, and both are readable by everyone with access to
# the repo. Instead a person or agent generates it locally, stores it as the repo
# secret TEST_INSTALLER_PASSWORD, and keeps a copy in a gitignored local file.
# This run then sets the account's password to that value, so the local copy and
# the account agree without the value ever crossing a log.
#
# That also gives a lost password a self-service fix that needs nobody's
# permission: generate a new one, `gh secret set TEST_INSTALLER_PASSWORD`, re-run
# this workflow. Redeeming the fresh code resets the account to the new value.
# Full instructions, including the exact commands: docs/test-account.md.
#
# On demand only. It creates and repairs a real auth user on the production
# project, and the account is durable — there is nothing to re-run on a merge.
#
# Nothing here prints a secret. The script asserts its work by effect: it signs
# in as the account, checks the database does not treat it as foreman or above,
# and writes a real install event to prove the exclusion that keeps its work out
# of the company's target times actually holds.

name: Provision the test installer login

on:
  workflow_dispatch:
    inputs:
      remove:
        description: "Delete the test login and its sandbox job instead of creating it"
        type: boolean
        default: false

permissions:
  contents: read

concurrency:
  # Shared with the foreman run: both touch the same sandbox job and the same
  # crew-invite machinery, and two at once would race over it.
  group: provision-test-accounts
  cancel-in-progress: false

jobs:
  provision:
    name: Create or repair the test installer account
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - name: Checkout
        uses: actions/checkout@v4

      - name: Create or repair the account
        env:
          SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN }}
          TEST_INSTALLER_PASSWORD: ${{ secrets.TEST_INSTALLER_PASSWORD }}
          # Production. Named explicitly for the same reason scripts/pgq.sh
          # refuses to guess one: a run against the wrong project would report
          # success while creating a login for a database nobody uses.
          SUPABASE_PROJECT_REF: czprjcskmzzagdztqonm
          REMOVE: ${{ inputs.remove }}
        run: |
          if [ -z "$SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN" ]; then
            echo "::error title=No test login was created::SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN is not set, so nothing could be created. It is the same secret deploy-backend.yml uses, so if that workflow works, this one has lost its copy."
            exit 1
          fi
          if [ "$REMOVE" = "true" ]; then
            scripts/provision-test-installer.py --remove
            exit $?
          fi
          if [ -z "$TEST_INSTALLER_PASSWORD" ]; then
            echo "::error title=No test login was created::TEST_INSTALLER_PASSWORD is not set, so this run had no password to give the account. Generate one locally and add it with: gh secret set TEST_INSTALLER_PASSWORD. See docs/test-account.md."
            exit 1
          fi
          scripts/provision-test-installer.py

      - name: Say what to do with it
        if: success() && inputs.remove != true
        run: |
          {
            echo "### The test login is ready"
            echo
            echo "Sign in at the app as \`qa.installer@crew.infinitywindows.app\`."
            echo "The password is whatever \`TEST_INSTALLER_PASSWORD\` holds — this"
            echo "run did not print it, and GitHub cannot show it to anyone."
            echo
            echo "It is an **installer**, it is flagged as a test account, and its"
            echo "work is excluded from every company-wide figure. Full notes,"
            echo "including how a local agent gets the password:"
            echo "**docs/test-account.md**."
          } >> "$GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY"
